   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1CH.18.1#p1-38a46f20",
     "text": "Which 2Sa 8:1 calls the bridle of bondage, because it was a strong town and kept the country around it in subjection.",
     "label": "a",
     "anchor": "Gath and her towns out of",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "2Sa 8:1",
       "ref": "2SA.8.1"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1CH.18.6",
   "range": "1CH.18.6",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "3e21abd6",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1CH.18.6#p1-3e21abd6",
     "text": "That is in all things that he attempted.",
     "label": "b",
     "anchor": "preserved David whithersoever he went"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1CH.18.8",
   "range": "1CH.18.8",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "37f900bb",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1CH.18.8#p1-37f900bb",
     "text": "Which in 2Sa 8:8 is called Betah and Berothai.",
     "label": "c",
     "anchor": "Tibhath",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "2Sa 8:8",
       "ref": "2SA.8.8"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1CH.18.10",
   "range": "1CH.18.10",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "d8b470e9",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1CH.18.10#p1-d8b470e9",
     "text": "Called also Joram 2Sa 8:10.",
     "label": "d",
     "anchor": "Hadoram his son to king David",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "2Sa 8:10",
       "ref": "2SA.8.10"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1CH.18.11",
   "range": "1CH.18.11",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "be77e7a3",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1CH.18.11#p1-be77e7a3",
     "text": "Because the Edomites and the Syrians joined their power together, it is said, 2Sa 8:12 that the Amramites were spoiled.",
     "label": "e",
     "anchor": "Edom",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "2Sa 8:12",
       "ref": "2SA.8.12"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1CH.18.12",
   "range": "1CH.18.12",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "0067dc8a",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1CH.18.12#p1-0067dc8a",
     "text": "Which is understood that Joab slew 12,000 as is in Ps 60:1 and Abishai the rest.",
     "label": "f",
     "anchor": "eighteen thousand",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Ps 60:1",
       "ref": "PSA.60.1"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
